<title>USA: AMBAC qualifies 14 muni bond issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>AMBAC qualifies 14 muni bond issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMBAC Idemnity Corp on Tuesday said that it qualifed for bond insurance the following 14 municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Allen County, Kan., Unified School District, $2.25 million General Obligations (GOs).</p>
<p>--Allegany County, Md., $6.68 million, Public Improvement bonds, direct purchase.</p>
<p>--Carver County, Minn., Housing and Redevelopment, $5.91 million.</p>
<p>--Conover, N.C., $2.5 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Garfield, N.J., $4.356 million, General Improvement bonds.</p>
<p>--Glens Falls, N.Y., School District, $8.5 million.</p>
<p>--Grand Island, N.Y., Central School District, $1.5 million.</p>
<p>--Cincinnati, Ohio, $47.3 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Horry County, S.C., School District, $22 million GOs.</p>
<p>--La Vergne, Tenn., $4.2 million, Water and Sewer Revenue bonds.</p>
<p>--Fort Bend, Texas, $5 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Deer Park, Texas, $4.12 million GOs</p>
<p>--Deer Park, Texas, $4.5 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Danville, Va., $6.55 million, General Improvement bonds.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
